        min_points=2,
        model_answer="Resistance is inversely proportional to cross-sectional area, and area is proportional to diameter squared. Doubling the diameter gives four times the area, so wire Y has one quarter of the resistance of wire X. If Y were also twice as long, its resistance would double, so it would then have half the resistance of X.",
